--TEST--
A `timeout:` that is not a duration or is zero, and an empty tag in `tags:`, are `E0880` at the value — `rule:testing/a-test-has-a-wall-time-limit`, `rule:testing/tags-and-shards-select-what-runs`
--FILE--
<?nvs
use Core\Test;

final class LimitTest {
    #[Test(timeout: "soon")]
    public function notADuration(): void {}

    #[Test(timeout: "0s")]
    public function zero(): void {}

    #[Test(tags: ["", "db"])]
    public function emptyTag(): void {}

    #[Test(tags: "db")]
    public function notAList(): void {}
}
--EXPECT--

--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0880]: `timeout:` is not a duration
%A
5 |     #[Test(timeout: "soon")]
  |                     ^^^^^^ this value
  = help: write a number and a unit, such as `"5s"`, `"250ms"` or `"2m"`

error[E0880]: `timeout:` is zero, so the test always fails
%A
error[E0880]: `tags:` has an empty tag, which `--tag` cannot select
%A
error[E0401]: expected `array<string>`, found `string`
%A
error: aborting due to 4 errors
To read what a code means and how to fix it, run `nvs agent show <code>`.
